// What a settlement is built of (terra_build::village, D229, D290): each of its builders'
// roles, construction materials by their files' names in data/kits, each building picking
// one of a role's by its seed; the roof over each of the first three is that material's own
// (`roof_kind`). Another people's village names others.
//
// The building baseline (D333) is wood and stone, and these are its materials: the fault
// ratchet (`cargo xtask artifacts`) and the QA films' sets (`cargo xtask qa`) are of what
// is named here. Earth, limewash, wattle and thatch are frozen, buildable by hand but in no
// role, so the cob and framed houses are built in stone and hewn timber.
(
    timber: ["logs"],
    masonry: ["stone"],
    beams: ["hewn"],
    cob: ["stone"],
    framed: ["hewn"],
    works: ["greystone"],
)
